#---
# purpose: "a self cycle with a constructor across it, closed through a value call rather than a named callee"
# defer: "compiling gloop/2 does not terminate: its return climbs one list layer per round -- int, int | [int], int | [int | [int]], 477 rounds and still climbing after 90s with the activation frontier growing one per round -- because the recursive call is made THROUGH a value, so it names no callee in any body, the static return-unknowns walk cannot see the cycle, and no component solve ever owns the return"
#---
def gloop(_f, 0), do: 0
def gloop(f, n), do: [f.(f, n - 1)]

def main() do
  dbg(gloop(&gloop/2, 2))
end
